# unit_cpu: unit tests (call) of S-CPU routines on paths no script reaches,
# from the start of a Novice race:
# - WindowStep3437By3 at $FE (held at $FF); BackdropAnglesFromView with
#   the view x $0664 = $C000 (the angle held at $E8);
# - WindowSlideUpSound with bit 2 of $0DA5; PlayerSound35 for player 0
#   with $0DF4 = 0; PlayerColoursFlash at level $A8 (the sum held at $FF);
#   WindowSweep with $0D62 set;
# - GaugeFromSpeed with no record ($02 = 0) and for the player's record
#   at speed $800 (held at $257); GaugeTableIndex for the vehicle kinds
#   $82E5 and an unknown one; PlayerVehicleRaised with bit 14 set in the
#   word its links lead to ($1A64).
# - ObjectSyncFromRecord for the player's car with bit 1 of its record's
#   +$1C; ObjectSpawnSparklePair with no free object (both spawns fail);
#   ObjectDrawListBuild with the car a kind-2 object with bit 6 of +$24;
#   DebugDrawChar for character 0 at $6400 on its second half (the cell
#   wraps); ObjectFree of the used list's head ($0001).
# - HudPanelsStep stage 2 with the marker at $FF (the column held at $FF);
#   SoundPortsSend with a direct byte for port 0, then port 1; RotateXY and
#   RotateXZFrom08 for every sign of the vector at four angles;
#   ObjectPlaceOnParent of object $2F79 on the car with bit 0 of its +$25
#   set, then for every sign of its offset.
# - CameraFollowStep ($1A64) in each mode bit and mode (bits 10-12), with
#   odd target speeds and $8000, and turns either side of the target;
#   BigSpritesRow5 with $0E5C clear; PaletteCourseLoad with $10DC set;
#   WindowSweepStep 0 on each half step, at its sixteenth step, and
#   turning at $F2.
# - routines nothing in the scripts calls: three of the renderer byte
#   setters, the bonus digits' bounce and full sizes (with $0E6C clear and
#   set), OamBlock123Left, Gauge6APlace and two sprite-text entries.
# - ObjectSpawnPuff with no free object; RecordNameStore3 and 6 (nothing
#   calls them); ChampionshipScreenStep with HUD mode 0 and the split window
#   not in state 5 (WindowClosedDigitStep returns).
# - RecordTagCar4 and 8 (nothing calls them); TimeBelowRecord with the
#   first byte higher, the second higher and all equal; GlyphSlideThree with
#   the glyphs $8006 and $800C.
# - PictureTurnStep with R held (the pace of 8).
# - PaletteFadeStep with a fade under way: four colours, each part up,
#   down or already there.
# - NmiFrameUpload at the stages nothing sets ($0E, $12, $16, $1A, $1E,
#   $20) and the split screen's stage 8.
# - GlyphSpritesDrawAll with $0FAE 0 (the last four 8 pixels left);
#   BcdToBinary of $1234, $0999 and $9999.
# - OamHideForHudMode in HUD modes 1, 2 and 3; OamStagePause2 with pad 2's
#   Select pressed and one frame of pause ($0D2D = 1).
# - OverlaySpritesStep in states 5 and 6 (x at $A0, then at $9B).
# - WindowClosedDigitStep in state 5 without the override (on to $07:EBDD,
#   the end of the race, which does not return: noreturn, 60 frames).
# - WindowSlideCheck with a slide under way: as the race leaves it; with
#   the colour level at $E1 (WindowHdmaFFD1), the player's Y below $19C9,
#   the top band moving within its limits and bit 14 set in the word the
#   links lead to ($1A64) for the first time (the low band restarts at $40,
#   limit pair 2 from $02); with the level reaching $E000 (the slide ends);
#   with the level at its $EF00 limit and bit 14 set again; with bit 14
#   clear after it was set (the low band restarts at $20).
# - RasterStage at the stages no script reaches (0, 2, $16, $18, $1A, $1C)
#   and stage $0E with $0D5C negative; WindowTable7F and its long form
#   called on their own.
# - CourseZoomFromSelection4 and CourseZoomFromSelection with a HUD mode
#   ($0D2B = 1) for course 4.
# - RecordTimeInsert with $0D24 = 3, and for course 0 with a time of
#   1'30"00 against records of 1'00"00 or 2'00"00: second place, third
#   place and none.
